{
  "action": "deliver_reel",
  "words": "Rita. It’s done. Don’t play it yet. Just get it to Pittsburgh.",
  "intention": "Secure the physical media containing Alma's final message and hand it to the person responsible for transmission, ensuring the recording survives the evening despite the station's open line and the festival noise.",
  "detail": "I walk past the glowing ballroom, ignoring the spectacle of the lights. I don't stop for the projectionist's speech or the crowd. I find Rita, who is likely near the patch board or the lobby exit, and press the small reel-to-reel cassette into her hand. I check that the tape is still in the case. I do not look at the camera. I do not smile. I turn and walk out the side exit toward my car, leaving the festival lights behind me."
}
